{"a_galaxy_workflow": "true", "annotation": "Phonetic research workflow consisting of forced alignment with the Montreal Forced Aligner, verification of the alignments in Praat, and vowel formant extraction with new FAVE", "comments": [], "creator": [{"class": "Person", "identifier": "0009-0009-5001-4180", "name": "Jessica Wallace"}], "format-version": "0.1", "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0", "name": "Phonetic Research Tutorial (MFA -&gt; Praat -&gt; new-FAVE)", "readme": "Tutorial showing how to use the Montreal Forced Aligner. It uses sample data that can be found on Zenodo. After uploading the data, the next step is to check whether there are any words that are not included in the dictionary (find OOVs). The next step is to then generate pronunciations of these words before merging them with the built-in dictionary. The phonetic transcriptions can be then aligned to the individual sounds in the audio file. These alignments must be verified in Praat to ensure accuracy. Finally, the vowel formant measurements are extracted using new-FAVE.", "report": {"markdown": "\n# Workflow Execution Report\n\n## Workflow Inputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_inputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow Outputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_outputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow\n```galaxy\nworkflow_display()\n```\n"}, "steps": {"0": {"annotation": "Upload the transcription", "content_id": null, "errors": null, "id": 0, "input_connections": {}, "inputs": [{"description": "Upload the transcription", "name": "Transcription (TextGrid)"}], "label": "Transcription (TextGrid)", "name": "Input dataset", "outputs": [], "position": {"left": 0, "top": 142.79308759585226}, "tool_id": null, "tool_state": "{\"optional\": false, \"tag\": null}", "tool_version": null, "type": "data_input", "uuid": "14226c7d-7410-4f46-8625-8b14d1e79189", "when": null, "workflow_outputs": []}, "1": {"annotation": "Upload the audio file", "content_id": null, "errors": null, "id": 1, "input_connections": {}, "inputs": [{"description": "Upload the audio file", 